# {{BRAND}}

This is a Mantle site. Start with only these authored surfaces:

1. the YAML file under `manifests/` — product, data, and API contract;
2. `src/index.ts` — Cloudflare Worker entry;
3. `src/handlers.ts` and nearby service/route files — only when present for
   custom business behavior.

Generated files under `.mantle/generated/` are reproducible; run
`pnpm generate` instead of editing them. Launch metadata under `.mantle/`
describes this provisioned instance and is not a second application contract.

Core owns the normal D1/KV/Auth/Admin/REST/Trigger/OAuth/MCP assembly. Using
the public low-level Mantle and Cloudflare exports is allowed when the product
needs it; reuse Core adapters and safety helpers instead of creating a parallel
stack.

The small default is not a lock. Former starter customization points map to:

- `src/mantle/config.ts` → façade options/typed `extend`, or the public
  low-level composition recipe for full control;
- full Kiwa source → edit `public/index.html`, or copy/eject only the selected
  version-matched overlay/component into project-owned source;
- overlay seeds → edit the materialized UI/content contract and use
  Admin/Staff MCP/Procedures for stored content;
- repo-local updater → the installed `mantle update` comparator.

Project-owned manifests, handlers, routes, UI, Wrangler config, and ejected
source are freely editable and must survive updates.

Before changing code, run `pnpm check`. Use the installed Core skills when the
task matches them:

- `.agent/skills/mantle-develop/SKILL.md`
- `.agent/skills/mantle-plugin/SKILL.md`
- `.agent/skills/mantle-theme/SKILL.md`
- `.agent/skills/mantle-update/SKILL.md`

Instance facts and the original handoff are in `.mantle/launch-state.json`,
`.mantle/features.json`, and `.mantle/handoff.md`.
